  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Thursday)\nIssued at 215 AM CDT Fri Aug 28 2026\n\nThe mid-level ridge will continue to dominate the weather across\nthe Southern Plains for the week ahead with only slight wobbles in\nits location forecast. \n\nBias-corrected probabilistic guidance (i.e., the National Blend \nof Models) indicates very little spread among the 10th and 90th \npercentile temperature forecast, which indicates high confidence \nfor above-normal temperatures in the upper 90s to mid 100s deg F. \n\nThis synoptic-scale pattern will also be unfavorable for rainfall \nwith drought conditions continuing to worsen across Oklahoma and \nnorth Texas. As a result, elevated fire weather conditions are \nlikely most days with the hot and dry conditions that are combined\nwith very dry fuels. The total fire environment (weather + fuels)\nwill be susceptible to initial attack fires to low-end large \nfires.\n\nMahale",
